### 2. CSS Classes

You can define CSS classes in a separate file and apply them to your components using the `className` attribute. This is a good way to separate presentation logic from your JavaScript code.

```jsx
// styles.css
.button {
  background-color: blue;
  color: white;
}

// App.js
import React from 'react';
import './styles.css';

function Button() {
  return <button className="button">Click me!</button>;
