Static is a keyword in C# that can be used to declare static members of a class. Static members are shared by all instances of the class. Static members are not associated with any instance of the class and are shared by all instances of the class.
Static members can be variables, methods, properties, events, etc.
Static members are useful when you want to share data or behavior among all instances of a class.
